Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/5] soc: qcom: geni-se: keep ACPI probe away from a missing SE clock

geni_se_resources_init() tolerates devm_clk_get("se") failing for an ACPI
device, but leaves se->clk as an error pointer and then unconditionally
calls devm_pm_opp_set_clkname(dev, "se"). On an ACPI device without a
clock provider that call fails with -ENOENT, so no ACPI GENI controller
(including the existing QCOM0220/QCOM0411 IDs) can probe. Before the OPP
conversion (Linux v7.0) the same error pointer reached clk_get_rate() in
geni_i2c_clk_map_idx() and faulted.

Treat an absent ACPI SE clock as firmware-owned: store NULL, which the
clock API accepts as a no-op and for which clk_get_rate() returns 0 (the
I2C driver then selects its 19.2 MHz table), and skip the OPP clock name.
DT behaviour is unchanged.

This replaces an earlier draft that rejected the error pointer in the I2C
driver; that approach would have turned the old fault into a probe failure
for every ACPI GENI I2C device. Compiled against Qualcomm qcom-next
a47c4c5aa with its published config; not booted.

---
diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c
index 7e2b1cc9c..0d6f98666 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c
@@ -1210,13 +1210,23 @@ int geni_se_resources_init(struct geni_se *se)
 				     "Failed to get optional core clk\n");
 
 	se->clk = devm_clk_get(se->dev, "se");
-	if (IS_ERR(se->clk) && !has_acpi_companion(se->dev))
-		return dev_err_probe(se->dev, PTR_ERR(se->clk),
-				     "Failed to get SE clk\n");
+	if (IS_ERR(se->clk)) {
+		if (!has_acpi_companion(se->dev))
+			return dev_err_probe(se->dev, PTR_ERR(se->clk),
+					     "Failed to get SE clk\n");
+		/*
+		 * ACPI firmware owns the SE clock and its rate. The clock API
+		 * treats NULL as a no-op, whereas an error pointer must not
+		 * reach clk_get_rate() or the OPP core.
+		 */
+		se->clk = NULL;
+	}
 
-	ret = devm_pm_opp_set_clkname(se->dev, "se");
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	if (se->clk) {
+		ret = devm_pm_opp_set_clkname(se->dev, "se");
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
 	ret = devm_pm_opp_of_add_table(se->dev);
 	if (ret && ret != -ENODEV)
